# Transport

## Wire contract

Ingest host: `https://ingest-<cell>.newtalaria.com` (or `dsn` / `baseUrl`). Header: `X-API-Key` only. Plain JSON — no `input` wrapper, no `__className__`.

| Signal | Route | Body |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Events | `POST /v1/events` | `{ "events": [ … ] }` |
| Spans | `POST /v1/spans` | `{ "spans": [ … ] }` |
| Replay start | `POST /v1/replays` | `{ replayId, sessionId?, url?, … }` |
| Replay segments | `POST /v1/replays/segments` | `{ "segments": [ { replayId, segmentIndex, gzipBytes (base64), … } ] }` |
| Replay finish | `POST /v1/replays/{replayId}/finish` | `{ reason? }` |

Errors: `application/problem+json` with `code`, `detail`, `requestId`. Legacy Serverpod bodies (`__className__`, `retry`) are still parsed when `code` is absent.

## Permanent ingest disable

Classify by problem `code` and `retry`, not HTTP 401/403 alone.

- Permanent codes (`invalid_key`, `not_found`, `insufficient_scope`, …) or `retry: false`: log once, disable events **and** spans **and** replay for this page lifetime
- Quota / rate-limit (`retry: true`, `quota_exceeded`) and 5xx: keep sending
- Missing scope (`lacks required scope` / `insufficient_scope`): disable that signal only
- Do not persist across a full page reload — a rotated key must work after deploy
